BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cvs-seminar-weller-gow-20260624
DTSTART:20260624T120000
DTEND:20260624T130000
SUMMARY:CVS Seminar: There's a cost to everything — Why Low energy light bulbs might be bad for your health? The vascular benefits of sunlight
DESCRIPTION:Joint talk from Richard Weller (Medical Dermatology, UoE) and Andrew Gow (Rutgers University). Title: There's a cost to everything. Why Low energy light bulbs might be bad for your health? The vascular benefits of sunlight.\nHost: Mark Miller.\nRichard Weller made the first description of large stores of nitrogen oxides in the skin and showed how solar UV radiation releases NO to the circulation and lowers BP. Andrew Gow will show recent data from their collaboration on how different properties of light affect the vasculature and NO system in human studies.\nSocial: Pizza in The Larder 13:00-13:30.
LOCATION:Wellcome Theatre, QMRI
STATUS:TENTATIVE
END:VEVENT
